<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of weekend</p>
<p>matches in the Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro soccer</p>
<p>championships.</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> Aracatuba		  1    Sao Jose		     0</p>
<p> Corinthians		1    Portuguesa		   1</p>
<p> Internacional Limeira  5    America/S.J.Rio Preto    0</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		 2    Guarani			2</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista    1    Palmeiras		    4</p>
<p> Rio Branco		 3    Botafogo/Ribeirao Preto  0</p>
<p> Santos		     1    Uniao Sao Joao	     1</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		  8    Juventus		     1</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p> Palmeiras		 18 11  6  1 46 20 39</p>
<p> Portuguesa		18  9  6  3 38 25 33</p>
<p> Santos		    18  8  7  3 32 22 31</p>
<p> Guarani		   18  5  8  5 34 40 23</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  18  3  7  8 23 34 16</p>
<p> Juventus		  18  3  6  9 31 46 15</p>
<p> Botafogo		  18  1  8  9 12 25 11</p>
<p> America		   18  2  4 16 14 47 10</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     18 10  5  3 45 23 35</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 18  7  9  2 35 18 30</p>
<p>Internacional Limeira 18  6  7  5 33 29 25</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  18  6  6  6 23 21 24</p>
<p> Rio Branco		18  6  6  6 24 24 24</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 18  6  5  7 22 24 23</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		18  5  7  6 24 28 22</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   18  5  5  8 24 34 20</p>
<p>Note: The teams play once against the other teams in their</p>
<p>own group, then twice against the teams in the other group. At</p>
<p>the end of this, the top two teams in each group qualify for</p>
<p>the final play-off stage. If teams are level on points,</p>
<p>positions are decided by the number of games won.   </p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, second stage</p>
<p> Bangu			0    Fluminense		   2</p>
<p> Botafogo		   1    Vasco da Gama		0</p>
<p> Flamengo		   3    Americano		    0</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	    2    Madureira		    1</p>
<p>Second stage standings</p>
<p> Botafogo		   6  4  2  0  8  4 14</p>
<p> Fluminense		 6  4  1  1  10 5 13</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	    6  3  1  2  5  4 10</p>
<p> Flamengo		   5  2  2  1 11  7  8</p>
<p> Americano		  6  2  1  3  7 10  7</p>
<p> Bangu			5  1  2  2  5  5  5</p>
<p> Madureira		  6  0  3  3  7 11  3</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	    6  1  0  5  6 13  3</p>
<p>Note: the winners of the first, second and third stages</p>
<p>qualify for the final round. Only the top eight in the first</p>
<p>stage go into the second stage and the top six teams in the</p>
<p>second stage carry on into the third stage. If the same team</p>
<p>wins all three stages, they become champions automatically.</p>
<p>First stage winners - Botafogo</p>
<p>Eliminated in the first stage - Itaperuna, America,</p>
<p>Olaria, Barreira.</p>
